From e1ffa45f9684458b370ab8ad3b97611916ff0ac1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:43:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Build the construct tree alongside the large-CFG feed

A source CFG within the relooper's cap first gets the raw relooper
feed and only then the construct tree. On macOS 27.2's uber fragment
shader the feed fails validation (a block before its dominator) and its
2,000-block graph is past what the relooper takes, so 2.9 s of feed ran
in series before the construct tree that is adopted.

What the construct tree builds does not depend on the feed, only
whether it is adopted does. Build it on a scoped thread while the feed
runs. If the feed is adopted, or fails in a way the construct tree cannot
fix, the thread stops at its next pass-phase boundary and its result is
dropped. Otherwise nothing cancelled it, so its verdict is the one the
sequential call reaches, and it is kept as that call's would be.
spirv-val scratch files get a name per call so two candidates can be
validated at once.

The shader's SPIR-V is unchanged, and translation drops from 6.1 s to
3.8 s on the little cores and from 2.9 s to 1.8 s on two big ones (17.0
and 7.9 s before either change). Peak RSS goes from 77 to 124 MB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
